course: dictionary
lesson: 12856
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The words around «engaged» are the clues. Read the whole sentence, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «My aunt got engaged last summer.» Here engaged means she has agreed to marry someone. The clue is the wedding talk and the word got, which goes with a big life event.
explain: «The toilet is engaged, so please wait.» In the UK, engaged here means someone is using it, so it is busy. The clue is that you have to wait. In the US, people would say busy or occupied.
explain: «Every pupil was engaged in the science project.» Here engaged means busy with and interested in an activity. The clue is that the pupils are working hard and paying attention.
fact: Engaged is the past form of the verb engage, so it can also mean something has already happened: «She engaged the brake.»
fact: «Engaged to» means you have agreed to marry someone: «He is engaged to Maya.»
fact: In the UK, «the line is engaged» means a phone line is busy because someone is already using it.
fact: «Engaged in» means busy with or interested in something: «engaged in learning.»
fact: When a machine part is engaged, it is locked into place, like the gears on a bike.
exercise: «My aunt got engaged last summer.» What does engaged mean here? | Has locked a gear into place | Has been given a present | Is very busy at work | *Has agreed to marry someone
exercise: «The toilet is engaged, so please wait a moment.» In the UK, what does this mean? | It is broken and needs fixing | It is clean and ready to use | *Someone is using it, so it is busy | It is open for everyone
exercise: «Every pupil was engaged in the lesson.» What does engaged in suggest? | *Paying close attention and taking part | Eating their lunch | Lost outside the classroom | Asleep at their desks
test: «The phone line is engaged, so try again later.» What does engaged mean? | Locked into place | *Being used, so it is busy | Pleased and happy | Very quiet
test: «The crowd was engaged by the magician's tricks.» What does engaged mean here? | *Held their attention and interest | Made them angry with the magician | Locked them in their seats | Hired the magician for the day
exam: «The engineer engaged the gears, and the big machine began to move.» What does engaged mean here? | Hired a new engineer | Stopped the machine working | Agreed to marry the machine | *Locked a machine part into place
